{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.sorting_color_energy","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.sorting_color_energy","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Units.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.GroupWithZero.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.ZMod.Basic"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.not_sorting_color_energy_of_free_data","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.not_sorting_color_energy_of_free_data","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/sorting_color_energy.lean#L165-L171","doc":"**The claim is refutable at freely-chosen eigenvalues**, which is why it is\nnamed rather than carried as a `sorry`.\n\nAt `q = 1` with both eigenvalues `0`, the first conjunct reads `0 = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.sorting_color_energy_of_heckeRelation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.sorting_color_energy_of_heckeRelation","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/sorting_color_energy.lean#L146-L163","doc":"**Item (1), derived.**\n\nIf both eigenvalues satisfy the Hecke relation, and each is known not to be\nthe *other* channel's value, then they are the manuscript's `q` and `−q⁻¹`.\n\nThe two `≠` hypotheses are the channel identification — which summand is\n`Sym²` and which is `Λ²`. That is what the missing representation theory\nwould supply; everything downstream of it is proved. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.sorting_color_energy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.sorting_color_energy","kind":"def","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/sorting_color_energy.lean#L133-L144","doc":"**Eigenspace decomposition with explicit Hecke eigenvalues**\n([`prop:sorting-color-energy`] item (1)), as a proposition over\ncaller-supplied data.\n\n`σᵢ` acts as `q` on `Sym²(V)` and as `−q⁻¹` on `Λ²(V)`.\n\n**Named, not asserted** — but, unlike the other carriers drained under this\nbean, it is also *derived* here, from the Hecke relation: see\n`sorting_color_energy_of_heckeRelation`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:sorting-color-energy","label":"prop:sorting-color-energy","md":"quantum-observable-universe/measurement-observation/sorting-color-energy.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.exists_heckeRelation_ne_both_of_zeroDivisors","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.exists_heckeRelation_ne_both_of_zeroDivisors","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/sorting_color_energy.lean#L116-L131","doc":"**`NoZeroDivisors` is load-bearing, and here is the counterexample.**\n\nIn `ZMod 8` with `q = 1`, the Hecke relation reads `(x − 1)(x + 1) = 0`, and\n`x = 3` satisfies it while being neither `q = 1` nor `−q⁻¹ = 7`.\n\nRecorded so the hypothesis on `eq_or_eq_of_heckeRelation` is justified by a\nwitness rather than by the docstring asserting it.\n\n`decide` here is arithmetic in an eight-element ring at one concrete point —\nthe finite-computation case AGENTS.md §1a explicitly allows, not a structural\nclaim pushed through the kernel evaluator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.eq_or_eq_of_heckeRelation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.eq_or_eq_of_heckeRelation","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/sorting_color_energy.lean#L102-L114","doc":"**They are the only roots** — the substance of item (1).\n\nA scalar by which `σᵢ` acts on a summand, satisfying the Hecke relation, is\nforced to be `q` or `−q⁻¹`.  `NoZeroDivisors` is doing real work: over a\ngeneral `CommRing` a scalar can satisfy the relation without being either\nroot. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.heckeRelation_neg_qInv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.heckeRelation_neg_qInv","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/sorting_color_energy.lean#L97-L100","doc":"`−q⁻¹` is a root of the Hecke relation — the antisymmetric eigenvalue. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.heckeRelation_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.heckeRelation_q","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/sorting_color_energy.lean#L93-L95","doc":"`q` is a root of the Hecke relation — the symmetric eigenvalue. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.heckeRelation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.heckeRelation","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/sorting_color_energy.lean#L85-L91","doc":"**The Hecke relation** at a scalar: `(x − q)(x + q⁻¹) = 0`.\n\nThe manuscript's ground relation for the generator `σᵢ`, evaluated at a\nscalar by which `σᵢ` acts on a summand. ","signatureChunk":0}]}